              from group-level activation maps provided by the Human Connectome
              Project across multiple domains (e.g., emotion, language, motor)
              and precisely characterizes the functional roles of specific
              brain regions, including the amygdala, hippocampus, and
              temporoparietal junction. However, NiCLIP showed limitations with
              noisy subject-level activation maps. NiCLIP represents a
              significant advancement in quantitative functional decoding for
              neuroimaging, offering researchers a powerful tool for hypothesis
              generation and scientific discovery.",
  journal  = "bioRxiv",
  month    =  aug,
  year     =  2025,
  keywords = "CLIP; deep learning; fMRI; functional decoding; large language
              model; meta-analysis",
  language = "en"
}

@ARTICLE{Flemyng2025-in,
